{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Vimalakoṇḍañña","html":"<article id='thag1.64'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.64 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.64 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Sattamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Seven </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vimalakoṇḍaññattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Vimalakoṇḍañña </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Dumavhayāya uppanno, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I arose from the one named after a tree; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>jāto paṇḍaraketunā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I was born of the one whose banner shines. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ketuhā ketunāyeva, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The banner killer has destroyed the great banner, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mahāketuṁ padhaṁsayī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>by means of the banner itself. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Vimalakoṇḍañño thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
